        <p><strong>Location:</strong> Monterey, California.</p>
        <p><strong>Year:</strong> 2021.</p>
        <p><strong>Organization:</strong> Reef Check California.</p>
        <p><strong>My role:</strong> underwater photogrammetry surveys and surface-area estimation from 3D reconstructions.</p>
        <p>For an urchin remediation study, I used underwater photogrammetry to estimate the surface area of rugose plots with uneven, complex surfaces.</p>
        <h2>Supporting the study</h2>
        <p>I documented plots and estimated their surface area.</p>
        <h2>From field images to measurements</h2>
        <p>Photographs became 3D models whose geometry supported plot-area estimates.</p>
